  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div id=\"\"> <p>APOD</p> <p>Astronomy Picture of the Day</p> <p> <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Discover the cosmos!</a> Each day a different image or photograph of our fascinating universe is featured, along with a brief explanation written by a professional astronomer. </p> <div><p><img width=\"6000\" height=\"4800\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=6000&amp;h=4800&amp;fit=clip\" alt=\"Bright stars and colorful nebulas shine on a dark field of stars. A small, dark nebula near the center looks like a horse's head.\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=6000&amp;h=4800&amp;fit=clip 6000w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=150&amp;h=150&amp;fit=clip 150w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=300&amp;h=300&amp;fit=clip 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=768&amp;h=4800&amp;fit=clip 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=1024&amp;fit=clip 1024w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=1536&amp;h=1536&amp;fit=clip 1536w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=2048&amp;h=2048&amp;fit=clip 2048w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=50&amp;h=50&amp;fit=clip 50w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=100&amp;h=100&amp;fit=clip 100w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=200&amp;h=200&amp;fit=clip 200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=400&amp;h=400&amp;fit=clip 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=600&amp;h=600&amp;fit=clip 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=900&amp;h=900&amp;fit=clip 900w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=1200&amp;fit=clip 1200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=2000&amp;fit=clip 2000w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion.jpg?w=1568&amp;h=4800&amp;fit=clip 1568w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 6000px) 100vw, 6000px\"><img width=\"6000\" height=\"4800\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=6000&amp;h=4800&amp;fit=clip\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=6000&amp;h=4800&amp;fit=clip 6000w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=150&amp;h=150&amp;fit=clip 150w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=300&amp;h=300&amp;fit=clip 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=768&amp;h=4800&amp;fit=clip 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=1024&amp;h=1024&amp;fit=clip 1024w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=1536&amp;h=1536&amp;fit=clip 1536w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=2048&amp;h=2048&amp;fit=clip 2048w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=50&amp;h=50&amp;fit=clip 50w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=100&amp;h=100&amp;fit=clip 100w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=200&amp;h=200&amp;fit=clip 200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=400&amp;h=400&amp;fit=clip 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=600&amp;h=600&amp;fit=clip 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=900&amp;h=900&amp;fit=clip 900w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=1200&amp;h=1200&amp;fit=clip 1200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=2000&amp;h=2000&amp;fit=clip 2000w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Horsehead_Nebula_Killion_annotated_large_font.jpeg?w=1568&amp;h=4800&amp;fit=clip 1568w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 6000px) 100vw, 6000px\"></p></div> <div> <p><strong>Explanation:</strong> Today's <a href=\"https://app.astrobin.com/i/ju7bwr?r=B\">image</a> could have been a painting. But what do these colors mean? The brightest star, left of the center, is blue <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2025-november-20-alnitak-alnilam-mintaka/\">Alnitak</a> (the Girdle): <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alnitak\">a triple star system</a> best known for being the easternmost star in <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/universe/stories/quick-reads/discovering-the-universe-through-the-constellation-orion/\">Orion's Belt</a>. The instantly recognizable shape of a dark horse's head at the center is the aptly named <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2025-september-2-the-horsehead-and-flame-nebulas/\">Horsehead Nebula</a>. It is about five light-years tall and lies approximately 1,500 light-years away. It is made of <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2025-december-10-the-horsehead-nebula/\">dust and gas</a> that obscure the red glow behind it, which is caused by hydrogen gas being ionized by the bright star <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigma_Orionis\">Sigma Orionis</a> at the top. The orange nebula with dark filaments on the left is the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flame_Nebula\">Flame Nebula</a>. Closer to the Horsehead, the blue <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/universe/stories/quick-reads/decoding-nebulae/\">reflection nebula</a> <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2023-november-20-the-horsehead-nebula/\">NGC 2023</a> is actively forming stars. The data for this \"painting\" were collected for almost six hours at the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utah\">Utah</a> <a href=\"https://utahdesertremote.com/\">Desert Remote Observatories</a>, but the equipment was <a href=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1596965349990-6d67ce6b0c1c\">remotely controlled</a> by the astrophotographer from his home, over 2,000 km away in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illinois\">Illinois</a>.</p><p><strong>Tomorrow's picture:</strong> what's next? </p></div> </div></div>",
